WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Who is this for?

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:04.552
Developers who build any code
in this workbook that calls

3
00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:08.063
Graph or Resource Manager, and
the reviewers who approve it.

4
00:00:08.063 --> 00:00:12.157
You'll want to read Python or PowerShell,
and know what an access token is;

5
00:00:12.157 --> 00:00:14.587
you don't need a tenant
until the second lab.

6
00:00:14.587 --> 00:00:17.372
The reviewer's question
is always the same:

7
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:20.713
which calls, with which
permissions, in which cloud.

8
00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:22.224
The call list answers it.

9
00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:25.622
And the app registration
itself is part of the answer:

10
00:00:25.622 --> 00:00:29.945
exactly the task's permissions, a
certificate or a managed identity,

11
00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:33.240
never a secret, registered
in the tenant's own cloud.
